  "comment": [
    "The verb lexicon for instruction-match. The hook reads the verb and object of what the user asked for, and the verb and object of the tool call about to run, and compares them. Nothing here describes a past failure.",
    "Python regexes for boundaries; verbs and stopwords are plain words, matched case-insensitive. Common typos are included because real prompts contain them.",
    "conflicts holds the only verb-class pairs a file or agent action can contradict. A read verb is never a conflict: a question about a broken thing is often a request to fix it."
